\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Cross-waveform check on the $(\ensuremath  {d_{L}}\xspace  ,\iota )$ bimodality: weighted joint posteriors from the unrestricted direct uniform-in-$d_L$ runs at IMRPhenomD\_NRTidalv2 (left; Mode-B-anchored heterodyne reference, s10) and IMRPhenomXAS\_NRTidalv3\xspace  \ (right; default GWTC-1 reference, s14). Both show the same two-peak structure with the Mode-B region $\ensuremath  {d_{L}}\xspace  <30\,\rm  Mpc$ carrying $0.43$ (IMRPhenomD\_NRTidalv2\xspace  ) and $0.32$ (IMRPhenomXAS\_NRTidalv3\xspace  ) of the posterior weight: the bimodality is robust across the NRTidalv2 $\to $ NRTidalv3 calibration. The smaller IMRX Mode-B weight is consistent with the tighter upper \ensuremath  {H_{0}}\xspace  \ tail under NRTidalv3 reported in Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref {sec:prior}.}}{6}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bimodality-waveform-check}{{3}{6}{Cross-waveform check on the $(\dL ,\iota )$ bimodality: weighted joint posteriors from the unrestricted direct uniform-in-$d_L$ runs at IMRPhenomD\_NRTidalv2 (left; Mode-B-anchored heterodyne reference, s10) and \IMRX \ (right; default GWTC-1 reference, s14). Both show the same two-peak structure with the Mode-B region $\dL <30\,\rm Mpc$ carrying $0.43$ (\IMR ) and $0.32$ (\IMRX ) of the posterior weight: the bimodality is robust across the NRTidalv2 $\to $ NRTidalv3 calibration. The smaller IMRX Mode-B weight is consistent with the tighter upper \hzero \ tail under NRTidalv3 reported in Section~\ref {sec:prior}}{figure.3}{}}
